{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"═══ SESSION: b690 root-caused & closed, 3768 closed, 9 new bugs found, STACK REBASED ONTO MAIN ═══\nWorktree /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-wt-provider-seam, branch feat/llm-provider-seam.\n**BACKUP REF before the rebase: `backup/pre-rebase-provider-seam` (7573c20a84). Keep it until the\nstack lands.**\n\n## STATE RIGHT NOW — read this first\n* **The stack is REBASED: 28 commits directly on origin/main, `main ahead: 0`.** lint + typecheck\n  clean, `docs/env-vars.md` regenerated and its drift gate green.\n* **NOT PUSHED YET.** A full `tests/unit` run was still executing when the session wound down\n  (`$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/postrebase.txt`). **Do not push until that is green** — the rebase involved\n  SEVEN hand-resolved semantic conflicts; nothing else in this session is as unverified as this.\n* Ten of my 38 pre-rebase commits were already on main (Gerrit rewrote their SHAs on submit, so\n  patch-id did not skip them) — a loop skipped them by Change-Id.\n\n## CLOSED\n**b690** (LLM-Review +1 / Verified +1, change 1178) and **3768** (change 1169). Closing 3768\nreported `UNBLOCKED: 0d76`, so the 0d76 -> eb6e -> 8625 chain is live again.\n\n## b690's ROOT CAUSE — not in any of the three seams its plan predicted\n`PydanticAIRunner.run` opened `cfg = self._config` and resolved the model from it, DISCARDING\n`req.config.model`. So `RunnerAgentStep` computed each step's declared class correctly and the runner\nthrew it away. Proven by experiment (spy `_pai_model`: request asked PER-STEP-MODEL, resolver got\nCONSTRUCTOR-MODEL), not by inference. Fix: `_effective_config` substitutes the per-call model into a\nCOPY of the config, following the contract `build_usage_limits` already documents\n(\"`self._config` is the floor; `req.config` is the per-call override\").\n**TWO CORRECTIONS to the prior investigation, both recorded on b690:** (1) H3 was eliminated on\nunsound reasoning — `_parse_slot`'s middle term is the deprecated bare `REBAR_LLM_MODEL`, so\n\"empty table => sonnet\" only holds when that is unset. (2) **This repo configures NO `model_classes`\ntable**, so `frontier` == the built-in opus default == `cfg.model` — six-plus of the nine original\nprobe rows carried NO information. Only `verify`/`coach` (declaring `standard`) ever discriminated.\nAny future probe MUST configure a table that differs from cfg.model.\n\n## THE BIG ONE — Pass-1 was silently downgraded FIVE WEEKS AGO (ticket 77ed, fixed, change 1199)\nPlan-review's Pass-1 FINDER generates the findings that gate every claim. Archaeology on the tracker\nsidecars: **115 reviews generated findings on OPUS up to 2026-06-27, then ZERO ever since** — a total\nchangeover one day after `4beec08a4` introduced `_verifier_cfg`. That commit downgraded Pass-2/Pass-4\nto the non-frontier model and its docstring asserts \"The Pass-1 finder is unaffected\"; the claim was\nFALSE from the moment it was written, because the downgraded cfg is passed as the WHOLE RUN's cfg at\nthe `produce_plan_review_verdict` boundary, the runner is built from it, and the runner discarded\n`req.config`. b690 is the ENABLER of the fix, not the cause: until it landed NO ladder rung could\nreach Pass-1 at all. Operator decision: **Pass-1 = `frontier`, Pass-2/Pass-4 = `standard`.** Entry\nrung set to `frontier`; ladder reduced to one rung because only `model_ladder[0]` is ever read.\n**I was wrong twice here** — first proposing `standard` (\"preserve today's behaviour\", which would\nhave ratified the regression), then asserting \"nothing on main intends opus\", which the sidecars\nrefute. Both from reading current code without checking history.\n\n## NINE NEW TICKETS, all from work the epic surfaced rather than speculation\n| ticket | what | state |\n|---|---|---|\n| **afeb** | 4 hand-built sub-calls bypass the class config; `overlap-judge` alone is 65% of a plan review's INPUT TOKENS on the frontier default; `ticket-digest` runs on the STORE WRITE path | fixed, 1194 + 1201 |\n| **8455** | a FAILED LLM call writes NO usage row (`record()` sits after the always-re-raising except spine) so spend totals under-report | fixed, 1195 |\n| **7a79** | cache warning fired below the 4096 floor; its own motivating example (4029 tokens) was itself sub-floor | fixed, 1193 |\n| **00da** | `rebar comment` stored a flag token AS the body and exited 0 — TWO defects stacked (also a surplus positional dropped by `args[:min_args]`) | fixed, 1197 |\n| **baa8** | live tier never reached the model; BOTH causes test-side (uncommitted prompt under the snapshot gate; a stale fixture tripping blocking P10) | fixed, 1196 (INDEPENDENT, on origin/main — needs 8070's helper) |\n| **03b0** | configured Bedrock provider silently dropped for canonical `...-v1:0` ids | fixed, 1189; stays OPEN pending child 7b22 |\n| **7de4** | `sizing.MODEL_LADDER` bare ids — context-limit escalation still bypasses the class table | FILED ONLY |\n| **7b22** | qualifier by registry membership not prefix shape (OSS consensus); child of 03b0 | FILED ONLY |\n| **8415** | overlap token cost; operator's design = move the shared digest into the system prompt | FILED ONLY |\nPlus unparented: **bb9b** (contributor re-trigger for fail-closed LLM-Review -1), **9416** (rename\n`verify.overlap_enabled` -> `suggest_duplicate_tickets`; undocumented outside the schema),\n**316a** (RETIRE `rebar review`, alias it to the plan-review verb — operator decision).\n\n## THE REBASE — what was resolved and what was DISCARDED\nSeven conflicts. **No behaviour was lost anywhere.** Verified, not assumed:\n* `1484` — main had INDEPENDENTLY split the same cluster into `plan_review_tail.py`. Operator chose my\n  verb-named `plan_review_recovery.py` (\"a split on a verb is more durable\"). Absorbed main's one\n  extra symbol (`_cancelled_plan_review_verdict`), DELETED `plan_review_tail.py` (1 importer, 0 test\n  refs). **This is the only genuine discard: main's module ORGANISATION, not its code.**\n* `172e` — kept BOTH my class-based model swap and main's `max_output_cfg`, ordered so the budget\n  raise follows the swap (main's own comment requires that order).\n* `e6bd` — took my extracted `interpret_failure` over main's inline spine. I initially only\n  spot-checked and CAUGHT that main's `format_repetition` was missing; re-added it. Then verified\n  EXHAUSTIVELY: 17 distinguishable behaviours in main's spine, all 17 present.\n* `b690`/usage_log.py — main's repetition helpers + my `record` signature (a strict superset).\n  **My \"keep both\" helper REFUSED to auto-resolve because both sides defined `record`** — without\n  that assertion I would have written two `record` definitions with the second silently winning.\n* `7a79`/pass1.py — my single-sourced floor + main's `_prefix_tokens`.\n* `f844`, and repeatedly, `docs/env-vars.md` — GENERATED; regeneration is authoritative.\n\n## GERRIT — 11 changes, NOTHING SUBMITTED\n1164 d23e · 1169 3768 · 1178 b690 · 1189 03b0 · 1193 7a79 · 1194 afeb · 1195 8455 · 1197 00da ·\n1199 77ed · 1201 afeb-followup, plus **1196 baa8 INDEPENDENT on origin/main**.\nAll patch sets predate the rebase, so **every one needs re-pushing** after the suite goes green.\n**TWO coverage-gap `-1`s occurred** (1189 PS1, 1193) — `review-error`, INFRA not findings.\nCONTRIBUTING §2c: not your code, a maintainer re-triggers, DO NOT amend the diff. 1189 PS1's `-1`\nbecame `+1` on re-review with the same code, which is the evidence bb9b is built on.\n\n## STANDING DECISIONS FROM THIS SESSION — do not relitigate\n* Pass-1 `frontier`; Pass-2/Pass-4 `standard`.\n* One-call top-level ops (`review_ticket`, `spec_scan`) keep the OPERATOR's `cfg.model` — the class\n  vocabulary is for differentiating passes INSIDE a gate. Both registered as by-design in the AST\n  guard. (Superseded in effect by 316a retiring `rebar review`.)\n* Sub-call classes: `ticket-digest` trivial, `overlap-judge` standard, `code-novelty` standard.\n* `:` stays the provider separator (pydantic-ai's own `KnownModelName` has two-colon entries).\n* **NO historical narrative in source comments** — dates, SHAs, run counts belong in tickets. I had\n  to strip this from the YAML, `_verifier_cfg`'s docstring and a test file after the operator\n  called it out.\n* Never trust `make lint | grep | head -1` — it matched `ruff check`'s \"All checks passed\" and\n  truncated before `ruff format`'s failure. **Check exit codes.**\n* A worktree without a venv fails the commit hook on `make typecheck`; that is environment, not code."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785640786000662001,"uuid":"5cde981b-ebe1-4996-883c-59aa7014e5a7"}